N2  - Study Objective: Demonstrate technique for myomectomy of a fibroid located within an isthmocele as well as repair for the isthmocele. Design: Case report Setting: Operating room, patient in dorsal lithotomy. Utilizing the robot and hysteroscopy. Patients or Participants: 41 yo G6P1052 with AUB-L (heavy menstrual bleeding and intermenstrual bleeding) with desire for future fertility who was found to have two fibroids, one of which was located within an isthmocele. Interventions: robot assisted lysis of adhesions, excision of possible endometriosis, myomectomy, chromopertubation, hysteroscopy, levonogestrel IUD insertion, and localizing ureteral catheter insertion and removal Measurements and Primary Results: n/a Conclusion: Demonstrates technique for myomectomy and repair of isthmocele.
