N2  - Study Objective: Describe surgical strategies for greater efficiency of robotic surgical correction of Isthmocele. Design: Case Report in a videoarticle presentation. Setting: The patient was in lithotomy position and a 4th generation robotic platform was used, with a right side docking of the 4 robotic arms and an accessory puncture with a 12mm disposable trocar for laparoscopic assistance. Patients or Participants: We present the case of a 33-year-old asymptomatic woman referred for evaluation following an incidental finding during routine examinations. She expresses a desire for a future pregnancy. Regarding obstetric history, she is primiparous, having undergone a cesarean section six years ago. Interventions: Surgical correction using a robotic approach with hysteroscopy assistance was proposed. Measurements and Primary Results: In this videoarticle, we described the surgical technique for isthmocele correction and highlight the use of fluorescence on the robotic platform to improve the technique. Conclusion: The use of fluorescence imaging combined with transillumination in robotic surgery enhances anatomical visualization, allowing for a more precise and complete isthmocele resection. This approach improves surgical efficiency and contributes to safer outcomes for patients.
