N2  - Study Objective: To review isthmocele findings and to describe a 10-step approach for the surgical repair of an isthmocele in a unicornuate uterus. Design: Narrated video footage. Setting: Single academic institution. Patients or Participants: 41-year-old female, G11P2183 with a history of unicornuate uterus and three prior Cesarean sections, who was referred from reproductive endocrinology and infertility for diagnosis of isthmocele. Patient elected for surgical repair of the isthmocele. Interventions: Robotic-assisted laparoscopic excision and repair of an isthmocele in the setting of a unicornuate uterus under hysteroscopic guidance. 10-step approach includes the following: 1. Hysteroscopy. 2. Uterine manipulator with cervical cup. 3. Vasopressin. 4. Lysis of adhesions. 5. Backfill bladder. 6. Develop vesico-uterine space. 7. Identify isthmocele. 8. Excise / Revise defect. 9. Closure of defect. 10. Cystoscopy. Measurements and Main Results: N/A. Conclusion: Isthmocele is a rare complication of Cesarean section which can cause future pregnancy complications and infertility issues. Correction of an isthmocele can be performed safely using a 10-step approach with robotic-assisted laparoscopy under hysteroscopic guidance.
