N2  - Study Objective: Video demonstration of robotic resection of uterine niche with use of ICG for identification of uterine defect. Step by step demonstration of the lower uterine segment defect. Design: N/A. Setting: Academic Medical Center. Patients or Participants: N/A. Interventions: Robotic Assisted Resection and Repair of Niche. Measurements and Main Results: Resolution of Niche as documented by Hysteroscopy. Conclusion: Robotic assisted technology can be used in a safe and reproducible manner in resection and repair of uterine niche defects. Additionally, ICG can be used to aid the identification of the defect intra-operatively.
