N2  - Cesarean scar pregnancy (CSP) is a rare form of ectopic pregnancy. We present two different techniques of laparoscopic management of CSP, with the concomitant repair of the coexisting uterine isthmocele. The first case is a combination of diagnostic hysteroscopy and laparoscopic extraction of conception products, and the second technique is a combination of laparoscopy and guided Dilation & Curettage. We also conducted a thorough review of the literature to present all cases of laparoscopic treatment of CSP, focusing on the surgical technique, the operation outcome, and the future pregnancies. Laparoscopy is a potential effective treatment of CSP.
