N2  - Today, operative hysteroscopy is an important part of gynaecological surgery. Due to many new developments more indications will be included. New indications are the hysteroscopic resection of retained placental products and in selected cases the hysteroscopic reconstruction of an isthmocele in caesarean section scars. Intrauterine shavers are new endometrium saving methods in the treatment of intrauterine lesions. Second generation of endometrium ablation will be used increasingly in the future. Postoperative prevention of adhesion after intrauterine adhesiolysis plays an important role.
