N2  - Clinical case of the complete failure of the uterine scar after cesarean section four years after the last birth. In past history of a patient there are two cesarean sections without complications. An ultrasound scan and hysteroscopy have revealed a defect in the musclular wall of the uterus, covered by the bladder. Metroplasty per vaginalis with a successful outcome has been performed. Conclusion: provided that certain conditions are met, metroplasty per vaginalis is characterized by minimal injuries in combination with adequate correction of isthmocele.
