N2  - Video Objective: The study objective is to evaluate the minimally invasive (Laparoscopic & Hysteroscopic) management of isthmocele in infertile patients and their short term follow up. Setting: Tertiary referral center (Tulip Multispeciality Hospital). Interventions: Seven patients who presented with infertility together with pelvic pain and abnormal uterine bleeding were taken. The diagnosis was made by transvaginal ultrasound, sonosalpingography, hysteroscopy or MRI. Laparoscopic resection of isthmocele was done. Conclusion: At our center the laparoscopic management of isthmocele with hysteroscopic assistance has given excellent results in patients of infertility and abnormal uterine bleeding.
