N2  - Objective: To describe the hysteroscopic removal of a malpositioned Mirena IUD embedded in the cesarean section scar. Design: Case report. Setting: Henry Ford Hospital (Detroit, MI), University-affiliated Hospital. Patients: A woman with an IUD embedded in her cesarean section scar. Interventions: Hysteroscopic removal of Mirena IUD embedded in cesarean section scar. Measurements & Main Results: Successful removal of malpositioned Mirena IUD. Conclusions: Hysteroscopic removal with scar resection is an effective minimally invasive approach to removal of a malpositioned IUD embedded in cesarean section scar.
